  "index": 18,
  "response": "**Optimal Crossing Sequence:**\n\n1. Farmer takes the chicken across the river.\n2. Farmer returns alone.\n3. Farmer takes the fox across the river.\n4. Farmer brings the chicken back.\n5. Farmer takes the grain across the river.\n6. Farmer brings the chicken back again.\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n* The chicken must be taken across the river first to prevent the fox from eating it.\n* The farmer must then bring the chicken back to avoid leaving the grain alone with the chicken.\n* The fox can then be taken across the river, but the chicken must be brought back to prevent the fox from eating the chicken.\n* Finally, the grain can be taken across the river, and the chicken can be brought back once more.",
